Software Testing Assignment
1. Homepage Review (Flipkart)

I opened the Flipkart homepage and noticed a few issues that could be considered defects.

Issue 1: Banner image loads slowly

The main banner took a few seconds to load completely.
I think this is a defect because users may not be able to see the latest offers immediately, which affects their experience.

Issue 2: Some product cards are not properly aligned

On scrolling through the homepage, a few product sections looked slightly misaligned.
This is a defect because it makes the website look less organized and less professional.

Issue 3: Search suggestions overlap with other content

When typing in the search box, the suggestion list sometimes covers nearby page elements.
This is a defect because it can make it difficult for users to select the correct option.


2. Difference Between Error, Bug, and Defect
Error

An error is a mistake made by a developer or tester while creating the software. It happens during coding or designing.

Example: A developer accidentally writes the wrong formula to calculate cashback in Paytm.

Bug

A bug is a problem in the software that happens because of an error. It causes the app to behave differently from what was expected.

Example: On Instagram, sometimes the Like button doesn't respond even after tapping it.

Defect

A defect is an issue that is found when testing the software. It means the software is not working according to the requirements.

Example: On IRCTC, the payment page sometimes freezes after entering the OTP.


3. App Not Working as Expected

A few days ago, I was making a payment using PhonePe. The money was deducted from my account, but the payment was shown as pending for a few minutes.

I think the reason was a technical limitation. It was most likely caused by a temporary problem with the bank server or network connection rather than a mistake made by the developer.


4. Risks in a Food Delivery App
I) Security Risk

If the app is not secure, hackers could steal users' personal or payment information. This would reduce customer trust in the app.

II) Usability Risk

If the app is difficult to use or the buttons are confusing, users may find it hard to place an order. This could make them switch to another food delivery app.

III) Performance Risk

If the app becomes slow during busy hours, users may not be able to place their orders quickly. Some users may even leave the app before completing the order.


5. Defect or Risk
(a) The "Book Now" button does not respond on mobile.

Answer: Defect

Reason: The button is supposed to work, but it doesn't. Since an existing feature is not functioning correctly, it is a defect.

(b) There is no logout option.

Answer: Defect

Reason: If the project requires a logout option and it is missing, then it is a defect because an important feature has not been implemented.

(c) The app sometimes loads slowly during IPL match days.

Answer: Risk

Reason: During IPL matches, many users may use the app at the same time. This heavy traffic can slow down the app, so it is considered a performance risk.
